      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T19:02:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In practice, this probably doesn\u0027t matter, but a thought occurred.\n\nIf two services are working together to build a record, then who should own that records lifecycle? Right now, if the target implementation says remove() the target record, then the controller implementation will lose that record and everything it contributed to it (i.e. Cat2).\n\nThe tedious, but best way to deal with this is probably to keep a set of requests and always update() when one is added or removed. A full record removal corresponds to no more requests for that type of record. You could also have a nuclear option for teardown time I suppose (basically this).\n\nAgain, probably not needed in practice, but I figured I\u0027d bring it up",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "ae69604334f3c1c09c2c48eb0dbe1b68e736885c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
