      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T19:02:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Perhaps in another iteration, but I feel like the proper abstraction here is just \"supported_features\" and not \"categories\" (which is secretly supported features, because categories are defined in the supported features section of the record and the constants used for \"categories\" in the stack include all the features, not just the four category bits) + \"is browsing supported.\"\n\nWe could use all the supported features bits to see if browsing is supported in AVRC_AddRecord, and use that to see if we should add the browse channel PSM. That\u0027s really just a very small logic refactor too, and probably doesn\u0027t even need a flag.",
      "range": {
