      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T19:02:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The context here is that the cover art entry in the Target record requires the PSM that the cover art OBEX service is assigned, but we don\u0027t have that until that service is started, way up in the Java stack. As such, there\u0027s a callback with the relevant info when it starts. We use the PSM to update the SDP record, and set the supported feature bit at the same time.\n\nThe Controller record doesn\u0027t need anything to be done dynamically, since all it has is some static feature bits.\n\nGiven that background, you may consider updating this function to be Target record specific in naming _and_ functionality. Same with the disable function below, as it looks like that also doesn\u0027t work/doesn\u0027t need to work for the controller record either",
